# Build context for the WEB image only. The api builds from ./api and reads
# api/.dockerignore instead -- Docker uses the ignore file at the root of the
# context it is given, so this one does not apply there.
#
# The Dockerfile copies its four files by name, so nothing below is strictly
# load-bearing. It is here because a secret must never enter a build context
# at all: anything sent to the daemon can end up in a layer or a cache mount
# after a one-line edit to the Dockerfile.
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
README.md
LICENSE
docker-compose.yml

# The api tree, including any local node_modules, is not part of the web image.
api
